.TH PORTARBITER 1 "2025-01-01" "portarbiter 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
portarbiter \- determine and resolve TCP port ownership safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portarbiter
.RI [ options ] " <port>"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B portarbiter
analyzes which entity owns a TCP listening port on a Linux system and
resolves it correctly.

Ownership is determined hierarchically:

.IP \[bu] 2
Docker containers and docker-compose projects
.IP \[bu]
systemd-managed services (real daemons only)
.IP \[bu]
raw user or system processes

By default,
.B portarbiter
runs in dry-run mode and performs no destructive actions.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --kill
Terminate the owner holding the port.
Without this flag, portarbiter only reports ownership.
.TP
.BR --force
Force termination.
For processes this sends SIGKILL.
For Docker containers this uses
.B docker kill
instead of
.B docker stop .
.TP
.BR --dry-run
Show what would be done without performing any action.
This is the default behavior.
.TP
.BR --yes ", " -y
Automatically confirm dangerous actions such as
bringing down a docker-compose project.
Required for non-interactive or CI usage.
.TP
.BR --version
Show version, git commit, and build date.
.TP
.BR --help
Show usage information.
.TP
.BR --check
Check mode.
Performs a policy evaluation only and exits with a status code.
No output is produced and no action is performed.
This mode is intended for scripting and automation.

.SH BEHAVIOR
.B portarbiter
never blindly kills supervisor services.

Examples of protected behavior:
.IP \[bu] 2
SSH user sessions are treated as user processes, not as
.B ssh.service
.IP \[bu]
Docker-published ports are resolved to the owning container or compose project,
not to
.B docker.service

Docker compose projects require explicit confirmation before being brought down.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
The operation would be allowed according to policy.
.TP
.B 10
Action failed.
The owning entity was identified, but termination failed.
.TP
.B 20
Action denied or confirmation required.
The owning entity is protected by policy or requires explicit confirmation.
.TP
.B 30
Detection failed.
The port could not be resolved to an owning entity.


.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Inspect port 5432:
.B
portarbiter 5432
.TP
Terminate the owning container:
.B
portarbiter --kill 5432
.TP
Force termination without confirmation:
.B
portarbiter --kill --force --yes 5432

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ss (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR docker (1)

.SH AUTHOR
Written by the portarbiter project contributors.

